# Vue / Inertia frontend

Follow `docs/project/CONSTITUTION.md` §§9–11. Facts: `docs/project/ARCHITECTURE_BASELINE.md`.

## Stack as it exists

Vue 3 `<script setup>` (JavaScript, not TypeScript), Inertia 2, Tailwind 3 utilities, Ziggy `route()`, `trans()` / `$t()` from `laravel-vue-i18n`. No Pinia. No ESLint/Prettier.

## Layouts and theme

- Admin pages: `AppLayout`. Public pages: `FrontendLayout`. Auth: existing Fortify cards.
- Do not introduce a new layout family without an ADR. Do not restyle by inventing a page-local palette; use tokens (`primary`, `surface`, `text-main`, `border`) from `tailwind.config.js` / `app.css`.
- Prefer in-use `Components/Base/*` (`BaseButton`, `BaseCard`, `BaseInput`, `BaseSelect`, `BaseList`, `BaseModal`, `BasePagination`). **Do not** promote unused `BaseSearchSelect` or `DashboardStatCard` to the design system. Do not add another button/modal family beside Jetstream leftovers unless the task is UI consolidation.

## Pages and forms

Pages compose features. Shared UI goes in `Components/`; shared logic in `Composables/`. Use Inertia `useForm` and show server `errors`. Client checks are UX only.

`usePermission` / `useNavigation` hide menus. That is **not** authorization.

New UI: loading/error states for mutations, existing `sm`/`md`/`lg` breakpoints, keep `sr-only` / `aria-*`. User-facing strings go through `lang/{locale}/sources` + `lang:merge`, not page-local maps.

After Vue/CSS changes, validate with `npm run build` (or `npx vite build`).
